    "groups": [
      {
        "group": "About audit actions",
        "items": [
          {
            "q": "What is a re audit in a care home?",
            "a": "It is a second look at something an audit found, to check the fix held. In CareStream the re check happens at the next run of the same audit, which lists last time's actions for the auditor to mark fixed or not fixed."
          },
          {
            "q": "What should an audit action plan include?",
            "a": "For each finding: what needs to happen, who owns it, how urgent it is and the date it is due. Then the outcome, ideally with a photo or note. CareStream actions carry an owner, a priority and a due date."
          },
          {
            "q": "How do I keep track of audit actions?",
            "a": "Use one action tracker, not notebooks and emails. Each action shows as open, in progress or done, and owners update it in the Staff Hub. Reminders go out when it is due soon and when it is overdue."
