    "heading": "A practical way to close the loop on audit findings",
    "lede": "Most services audit well. The weak point is the stretch between a finding and proof it was closed. A few small habits make that stretch visible.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "h3": "Write the action while the finding is fresh",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Do it before you leave the corridor. An action written on the day has an owner and a date, and a verbal word does not. Keep the wording specific: not \"sort the handrail\" but \"refix the first floor corridor handrail by Friday\". If the fault cannot wait, give it the top priority and make the owner aware straight away.",
          "Decide what proof you expect for each kind of action. A repair suits a photo. A review suits a short note. Agreeing this in advance makes the audit evidence consistent from one audit to the next."
        ]
      },
