   {
    "h3": "Training evaluation that fits a busy service",
    "paragraphs": [
     "Evaluating training effectiveness does not need to be complicated. The Kirkpatrick model, a widely used way of measuring training effectiveness, separates four things: whether people liked the session, whether they learned from it, whether they now act differently on the floor, and whether outcomes improve. Feedback forms cover the first. A knowledge check after the session covers the second. Observation and audits cover the rest."
